But even with this system, there is still a penalty going from hat
trick with bells (10 points) to grand slam without bells (6 points),
among other things.

What about something a little simpler... just give points for a
person's highest award with bells and their highest without bells,
using the current scoring system. If these are the same, they get both,
i.e. three appropriate ascensions in a row would give 12 points (4
points for double top + 8 points for double top with bells), while two
opposite gender ascensions in a row plus a third appropriate ascension
would give 10 points (4 points for double top + 6 points for birdie
with bells). This would eliminate that problem without having to add
another layer of complexity to the scoring system.

Also, giving some amount of points per ascension might help motivate
people, since getting from a hat trick to a grand slam is quite a bit
of effort with basically no reward in between.

Either or both of these ideas may require either scaling down the
scoring for the recognition trophies or reevaluating the scoring for
the major trophies to get them back into a reasonable ratio, but I
think they would overall make a system that makes more sense.

